{"name":"Vintage Beige","hex":"#dfe1cc","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vintage","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The yield of grapes or wine from a vineyard or district during one season.","Wine, especially high-quality, identified as to year and vineyard or district of origin."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to a vintage, or to wine identified by a specific vintage.","Having an enduring appeal; high-quality."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vintage"},{"term":"beige","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour, variously defined from a pale brown, to a yellow greyish off-white.","Debeige; a kind of woollen or mixed dress goods."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a slightly yellowish gray colour, as that of unbleached wool.","Comfortably dull and unadventurous, in a way that suggests middle-class suburbia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beige"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vintage","blocks":[{"text":"In winemaking, vintage is the process of picking grapes to create wine. A vintage wine is one made from grapes that were all, or primarily, grown and harvested in a single specified year. In certain wines, it can denote quality, as in Port wine, where Port houses make and declare vintage Port in their best years. From this tradition, a common, though not strictly correct, usage applies the term to any wine that is perceived to be particularly old or of a particularly high quality."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Cup_vintage_Cdm_Paris_320_n1.jpg/330px-Cup_vintage_Cdm_Paris_320_n1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vintage","wikidata":"Q1975981"},{"title":"Beige","blocks":[{"text":"Beige is variously described as a pale sandy fawn color, a grayish tan, a light-grayish yellowish brown, or a pale to grayish yellow. It takes its name from French, where t